/**
 * @file modules.dox
 * @brief Declares the module tree used by @c \@ingroup throughout the sources.
 *
 * Keeping the group definitions in one file (rather than scattered across
 * whichever header happened to be documented first) makes the hierarchy easy to
 * see and to reorder.  Sources only ever @c \@ingroup or @c \@addtogroup these.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup fcbus Famicom bus interface
 * @brief Everything that moves bytes between the 6502 and the RP2350.
 *
 * The cartridge presents itself to the console as CHR-ROM on the PPU bus.  Four
 * PIO state machines handle the electrical protocol, one DMA channel feeds the
 * outgoing byte stream, and a 64-byte mailbox riding on the tail of each frame
 * carries commands in both directions.
 *
 * @see @ref protocol
 * @see @ref nes_doom
 */

/**
 * @defgroup platform Platform and runtime
 * @brief Board bring-up, dual-core scheduling, watchdog and debug tracing.
 * @see @ref architecture
 */

/**
 * @defgroup graphics Graphics pipeline
 * @brief Software rasteriser, OpenGL subset and the framebuffer-to-PPU converter.
 *
 * Rendering happens entirely on core 0 into a linear 8-bit canvas, which is then
 * transposed into the two-bitplane layout the PPU fetches.
 *
 * @see @ref graphics_page
 */

/**
 * @defgroup audio Audio pipeline
 * @brief NSF playback via an emulated 6502, relayed to the console's real APU.
 * @see @ref audio_page
 */

/**
 * @defgroup app Application layer
 * @brief The tutorial sketch: scene state machine, resources and title screen.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup bootrom 6502 boot ROM
 * @brief Code that runs on the console's own CPU.
 *
 * Split into two independently assembled halves: the erasable main bank
 * (@c BOOTROM/, `$8000`-`$EFFF`) and the permanent fix bank
 * (@c BOOTROM_FIX/, `$F000`-`$FFFF`) that owns the reset vectors and the
 * flash-programming routines.
 *
 * @see @ref boot_reflash
 */

/**
 * @defgroup toolchain Build toolchain
 * @brief Assembler, MML compiler, binary converters and cartridge flasher.
 * @see @ref build_pipeline
 */
